{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730070Z","id":"47eb01b7fd5fc3eb85b2d44bde1ae8b41029603afd1dda5c7f5fb072411419ac","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:114 (Q1)): doctor prints the approval line and never writes it. Writing it needs a comment-preserving TOML edit in clax init and a matching removal in clax uninit; the doctor's mcp detail and the READMEs then change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"ab384b31d810513ba2793692a27f8dac0f9118459eeaf07fe63eb2939829ea9f"},"summary":"Have clax init write Grok's tool approval, MCPTool(clax_grok__*), into ~/.grok/config.toml","tags":["revisit:the owner wants clax init to lift Grok's per-call approval","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730170Z","id":"913befb96284920adcabfe68b2fb7927291da171c7a5df898fa5236a66365606","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:113 (Q3)): Grok Build 1.0.45 and later, warned by doctor only (MIN_GROK). A different minimum changes this warning and the contract's measurement line; enforcing it would add a version check to the shim or the hooks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":550},"end":{"line":552},"content_hash":"08f4786b8e87c9b1ee9c6633438a61b1ef298ae07c9c75f84ab8067ba94831bc"},"summary":"Enforce a minimum Grok Build version instead of warning in doctor only","tags":["revisit:a Grok Build release older than MIN_GROK breaks Clax in the field","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697602Z","id":"953ed568ee63d900d24099459ad9eac9cefb3b71428050791cb057b21f68208e","body":{"detail":"Failure: after an upgrade, before the daemon is replaced, `clax doctor` runs Store::open, which plans and records the backfill (seconds on a large home, with no progress shown). Changes the still-running older daemon makes after that plan are never recorded: they are not in the staging snapshot, and the older build records nothing live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":613},"end":{"line":613},"content_hash":"e8cfaa20dc14468f4bef01aba5ada983db7554d9886c28787dbaec157f0587e0"},"suggested_fix":"Have doctor and init open the store without the backfill (or read-only) when the schema is behind and a daemon is running, and leave the backfill to the daemon's start, which reports progress.","summary":"clax doctor (and clax init's credential revoke) open the store directly, so the first run of a new build migrates to 23 and runs the whole backfill outside the daemon, silently, possibly under an older running daemon","tags":["review","migration","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:06:06.687692Z","id":"d2386e4668a1db08b83107394256621eb35a796e99cf86d2e5d8060ff546220f","body":{"detail":"Spec section 6.7 has a remote person's `agents` and `status` list the person's own agents through GET /api/agents, which plan Task 16 adds; it does not exist yet. GET /api/sessions?live=true answers a grant with its own grant's sessions only, so a person with two machines sees one machine's agents, and the owner sees the token's sessions. Switch agents_of to GET /api/agents when Task 16 lands; crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs remote_cli_commands_work_as_listed asserts the listing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"035c183d3a6be59d25aaa64b5804fd572d3599590675c6439571b9ea7a6f1271"},"summary":"clax agents and the remote clax status list this credential's sessions through GET /api/sessions, not the person's agents through GET /api/agents","tags":["spec:6.7","revisit:GET /api/agents exists","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:06:06.687756Z","id":"53080db307210215f653922a96822d22d16804a28173b33faa7b39cc51d91526","body":{"detail":"The continuation that issues tokens also rotates the continuation token, so a poll whose answer is lost leaves the client with a token the daemon no longer knows (401 invalid_token, or 409 already_issued). clax connect then forgets the request and its key and tells the person to have the owner revoke the connection in People; the next connect makes a new key and request. The stray grant signs nothing without the key. A retry that re-issues to the same key (an idempotent issue) would let the client recover without the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":353},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"38a5aeac6bc7aaf40772b6316b28717047bfaf09232aa277f3bb3826a9b77aca"},"summary":"A request whose tokens were issued to an answer that never arrived cannot be finished: its grant stays live until the owner revokes it or 30 days pass","tags":["spec:6.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.492338Z","id":"672e8ed0336b2436832365a5e5941505628838622e507ecf33ce60da41456ad6","body":{"detail":"The continuation that issues tokens also rotates the continuation token, so a poll whose answer is lost on the wire leaves the client with a token the daemon no longer knows (401 invalid_token, or 409 already_issued). clax connect then forgets the request and its key and tells the person to have the owner revoke the connection in People; the next connect makes a new key and request. The stray grant signs nothing without the key. An answer that did arrive is never lost here: remote-pending.json is removed only after remote.json is saved (both written whole by write_private). Recovery today needs the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":406},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"38a5aeac6bc7aaf40772b6316b28717047bfaf09232aa277f3bb3826a9b77aca"},"suggested_fix":"Idempotent re-issue: keep the hash of the pre-issue continuation token until the access token is first used (at most 10 minutes); a continuation call presenting it, signed by the grant's key with a later t, revokes the undelivered tokens and issues fresh ones in one transaction. Safe because the tokens are key-bound: a sniffer of the old token cannot sign, and accept_t refuses a replay.","summary":"A request whose tokens were issued to an answer that never arrived cannot be finished: its grant stays live until the owner revokes it or 30 days pass","supersedes":"53080db307210215f653922a96822d22d16804a28173b33faa7b39cc51d91526","tags":["spec:6.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
